Four unique Triton Amulets originally belonged to the famous [[Alexander the Great]], who used them to guard the underwater ruins of the legendary Lighthouse of [[Alexandria]] in [[Egypt]]. Their presence beneath the waves inspired the historical legend of four massive sea juggernauts protecting the structure. After Alexander's death, all four amulets remained sealed deep beneath the ocean floor. {{source|The Treasures of Alexandria}}

Many centuries later, the Huntik Team discovered the hidden chamber housing the artifacts. By solving a series of ancient riddles, [[Sophie Casterwill]], [[Lok Lambert]], and [[Dante Vale]] successfully recovered the first three Triton amulets respectively. However, [[Captain Caine]] of the Organization managed to seize the fourth Amulet. 

Lok and Sophie invoked their newly acquired Tritons for an underwater battle against Caine, who summoned his own Triton along with [[Megladeath]]. Dante subsequently gave his unused Triton Amulet to [[Zhalia Moon]], as only Seekers physically carrying a Triton Amulet could safely pass through Alexander's magical energy barrier back to the surface. When Caine returned to the surface, he gave his Triton Amulet to [[Gregor]], having completed his mission to obtain it. However, Dante, having escaped by using [[Metagolem]] to shatter the force field, used [[Farslip]] to take the Amulet from Gregor, ensuring that [[the Organization]] left empty-handed. {{source|The Treasures of Alexandria}}

Lok later summoned his Triton to battle [[the Organization]] on the Island of Sinbad, using its aquatic skills to disrupt the boat of Captain Caine and his [[Suits]]. {{Source|HM07}}
